1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,143
Welcome to Recon Forge, a governed policy evolution application for

2
00:00:04,143 --> 00:00:08,286
transaction reconciliation. It compares internal ledger records with processor settlements,

3
00:00:08,286 --> 00:00:12,429
identifies unmatched transactions, and helps operators improve matching rules using

4
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:16,571
measured evidence. This demonstration uses synthetic data with four familiar

5
00:00:16,571 --> 00:00:20,714
processor labels: Stripe, Adyen, PayPal, and Square. The dashboard shows

6
00:00:20,714 --> 00:00:24,857
ingestion progress, open breaks, the active policy, and accuracy measured

7
00:00:24,857 --> 00:00:29,000
on a fixed historical benchmark.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,143
The policy history view makes every change traceable. Here, approved

9
00:00:34,143 --> 00:00:38,286
versions have increased benchmark accuracy from twenty to forty percent.

10
00:00:38,286 --> 00:00:42,429
Each processor has explicit settings for amount tolerance, settlement timing,

11
00:00:42,429 --> 00:00:46,571
fixed fees, and percentage fees. Diagnosis identifies recurring failures, analysis

12
00:00:46,571 --> 00:00:50,714
checks evidence and verified memories, and evolution proposes a bounded

13
00:00:50,714 --> 00:00:54,857
change. The agent follows its policy skill and rules, changing

14
00:00:54,857 --> 00:00:59,000
one supported parameter at a time.

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,625
Human approval is the control point before a candidate becomes

16
00:01:03,625 --> 00:01:07,250
active. The review view compares current live accuracy with the

17
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:10,875
active and candidate backtest results. A compact diff highlights the

18
00:01:10,875 --> 00:01:14,500
affected parameter, with red for the previous value, green for

19
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:18,125
the proposed value, and line numbers for context. Clicking approve

20
00:01:18,125 --> 00:01:21,750
records the decision first. A persistent confirmation then tracks the

21
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:25,375
next steps, so operators can see that their decision was

22
00:01:25,375 --> 00:01:29,000
saved.

23
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,625
The workflow view explains what happens after approval. Promotion activates

24
00:01:33,625 --> 00:01:37,250
the eligible policy, replay checks it against held out data,

25
00:01:37,250 --> 00:01:40,875
and verified learning is saved for future incidents. Four visible

26
00:01:40,875 --> 00:01:44,500
progress stages distinguish queued work, active processing, and completion. If

27
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:48,125
replay fails its safety checks, the application can roll back

28
00:01:48,125 --> 00:01:51,750
the candidate. Data ingestion runs independently of this workflow, so

29
00:01:51,750 --> 00:01:55,375
transactions can keep arriving while a policy is being reviewed

30
00:01:55,375 --> 00:01:59,000
or verified.

31
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,625
Backtesting measures improvement before a change reaches the active policy.

32
00:02:03,625 --> 00:02:07,250
The independent historical benchmark contains eight thousand pairs, while the

33
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:10,875
live stream has been extended to twenty five thousand. The

34
00:02:10,875 --> 00:02:14,500
synthetic scenarios include settlement delays, fee differences, amount drift, reference

35
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:18,125
errors, and duplicate allocation ambiguity. Guardrails check false matches, regressions,

36
00:02:18,125 --> 00:02:21,750
and improvement. Candidate backtest accuracy is a projection for that

37
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:25,375
candidate; it becomes an active result only after approval and

38
00:02:25,375 --> 00:02:29,000
successful verification.

39
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,625
The reconciliation view connects policy evolution to operational outcomes: matched

40
00:02:33,625 --> 00:02:37,250
transactions, outstanding amounts, processor summaries, and unresolved cases. Long term

41
00:02:37,250 --> 00:02:40,875
Mongo database storage retains policy versions, human decisions, evaluation results,

42
00:02:40,875 --> 00:02:44,500
verified memories, and audit history. Raw demo fixtures remain local,

43
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:48,125
and routine telemetry expires automatically. Python code and fuzzy reference

44
00:02:48,125 --> 00:02:51,750
evolution are reserved for a later stage. Recon Forge demonstrates

45
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:55,375
a controlled learning loop: observe failures, propose a small change,

46
00:02:55,375 --> 00:02:59,000
measure it, approve it, and verify the outcome.
